WEBVTT

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.050
This chemical sweetness!

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:13.820
I love it!

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.270
Don't eat too much of that stuff, Mia.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.480
"Enjoy the little day-to-day 
happinesses while you can."

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.160
My dad told me that before he died.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.210
Want some, Julia?

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.350
No.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.420
You know I'm on a low-carb diet.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.880
Anyway,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.840
Rapture's back on the front lines.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.400
Huh...

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.260
Tamara is still with the Spetsnaz, right?

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:42.980
Yes.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.070
Rapture,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.110
War Nurse,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.480
Phoenix...

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.710
Four of the Magical Five have
returned to the battlefield.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.400
So now it's just Peipei, huh?

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.850
I kind of want to see her,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.200
and I kind of don't.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.150
You may get your chance
to see Rapture and War Nurse.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.530
I see.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.240
Your next mission is probably
going to take you to Japan.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.200
I can't wait.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.020
<b>Wish Upon a Star</b>

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.680
Excuse me,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.200
um...

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.920
I can't speak English.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.610
What?

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.190
Um...

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.380
Do you need help?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.280
Thank you!

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.430
I want to go to this hotel.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.450
It's just down that road.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.170
Okay?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.220
Okay!

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.250
Thank you!

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.110
Thank you!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.680
Bye-bye!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.710
Oh no!

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.350
Thanks for coming to my study group today!

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.440
Kurumi says she'll be late.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.150
Nozo-chan said the same thing.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.240
Okay,

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.480
let's start without them.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.320
Okay.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.820
This place has a ton of books, huh?

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.650
Lots of plays and books about drama.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.950
I can tell you're in the literature club.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:46.970
You know,

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.870
when you've read enough books,
you start to want to write one.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.090
I'm hoping I can be a
scriptwriter when I grow up.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.720
Is that your dream?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.450
Um...

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.230
What's your dream, Asuka-san?

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.010
My dream...

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:17.980
I don't really like myself that much...

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.010
So I don't really have a dream.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.560
You're wonderful, Asuka-san!

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:31.120
So don't say you don't like yourself.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.020
Nozo-chan, knock it off!

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.930
H-Hi!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.380
Kurumi?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:50.970
Asuka-san!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.150
Are you okay?

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.850
Did anything weird happen
between you and her?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.720
Anything... weird?

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.030
Um...

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.040
I think this is...

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.290
You use this formula to solve that one.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.160
Oh, I see.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.250
I can't do this! It's exhausting!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.260
It hasn't even been 30 minutes, Nozo-chan.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.580
But I'm tired!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.740
I know!

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:23.020
Once this is over,

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:24.590
want to go to the Tanabata festival?

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.030
Tanabata festival?

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.760
They're doing it at the shopping
district in front of the station.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.440
There're lots of little stalls,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.890
and I guess it might be fun.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.660
I haven't been to a thing like that in ages.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.920
Then let's go!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.900
We can study better when we've
got something to look forward to!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.660
I'm fine,

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.100
but I think Kurumi had something to do.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.320
My schedule just opened up!

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.190
I'm prioritizing seeing you in a yukata...

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:54.740
I mean, making memories with my friends.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.530
I-I see.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.790
Okay, I guess we can.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.910
Hooray! Festival time!

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.970
Leonid Greenburg...

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.510
A Jewish-American mathematician.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.430
He was killed in Mexico,

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.050
and his brother's in Japan.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.840
Leonid's younger brother, Jerome,

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.750
is a millionaire who runs an IT company.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.550
Or, well, he's retired now
and living a comfortable life.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.190
He was.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:32.530
Now nobody can get a hold of him.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:37.800
The CIA's Japanese branch sent
up a micro drone to look into his room,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.510
and found him embedded in a cube.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:47.930
So a fairly powerful, illegal Magical Girl
 is involved in this matter, then?

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.890
Or a magical mercenary.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.530
Those Babel Brigade guys?

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.720
Good, this'll be fun.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.690
What will you do if you run into Rapture
and War Nurse during your investigation?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.640
I won't let them get in the way of my work.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.840
That's all.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:15.370
Shin Ookubo Terror Incident
 Were Illegal Mages Involved?

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.840
<i>Regarding the possibility
that illegal mages</i>

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.380
<i>were involved in the Shin
Ookubo terrorist incident,</i>

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:23.210
<i>opposition parties are blaming
the government's weak—</i>

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.170
Asuka and Kurumi-chan are late.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.650
I think they should be here soon.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.820
S-Sorry.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.900
I told her I didn't need
a fancy yukata, but...

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.180
Kurumi insisted...

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.730
I think it suits you best!

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.140
I agree!

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.000
Let's go, then!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.720
It's really close!

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.400
It's so exciting, going to
 a festival with everybody!

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.410
Huh?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.360
Where's Nozomi?

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.400
I can't eat anymore...

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.330
You eat too fast!

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.170
When did she eat all that?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.880
I'll watch Nozomi-san.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.600
We'll catch up with you later.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.240
Thanks.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:09.170
Sorry to ask.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.680
Your lap feels so good.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:20.000
It feels like you're used
to taking care of people.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.850
Maybe I am.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:26.460
Ever since you two transferred here,

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.310
every day has been such fun.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.810
You're right.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.700
You know,

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:38.160
Asuka and Sayako kind
of look like a couple, don't they?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.770
As her childhood friend,
it's kind of a good thing,

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.460
but it also makes me kind of sad.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.420
Let's get going.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.880
But my stomach still hurts.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.340
I don't care!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.520
Are you okay?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.790
Yes...

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:23.670
Excuse me.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:25.900
Yoshino-san?

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.960
Hi there.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:31.000
You guys?

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:41.200
Why is M Squad here?

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.680
I said I was off today.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.650
So are we.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:50.680
Iizuka-san gave us
the rest of the day off.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:53.360
He told us to go enjoy the festival with you.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:03.480
Part of the job when you work for
the JSDF is taking breaks when you can.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.080
Hey,

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.350
Asuka!

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:08.790
Introduce us!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.910
You know them?

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.630
Are they relatives of yours or something?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.340
No, we're...

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.570
<i>That was a really hard punch.</i>

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:25.470
We go to the same training
gym as Asuka and Kurumi.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.310
Oh, I see!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.640
I know!

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.650
Why don't we all go around together?

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.830
We'll use our grown-up powers to pay!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.720
Hooray!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.320
She never learns.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.250
When did it get so late?

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.250
Where did that weird group of people go?

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.580
They're in line to get beer and yakitori.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.910
Oh...

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:12.230
They look like normal teenagers
when they're like that.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.440
We don't look like soldiers
 right now ourselves.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.940
Soldiers, huh?

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.410
We enlisted voluntarily
and we're paid for by tax dollars.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.740
We're not like them.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:30.110
What will happen on our next mission?

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:31.840
I don't know,

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.380
but it won't be easier than what
we've dealt with up until now.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.170
I hope this isn't our last summer vacation.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.460
Don't even say stuff like that!

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:50.260
There's been so much
violence in the news lately.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.900
What's gotten into you?

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.520
When I'm in big crowds,

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.870
I start having flashbacks...

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.210
To when the Magical Girl saved me.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:04.610
There was a big fight
in Ookubo a while back, too.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.300
I hope the peace lasts forever.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.540
But I think it won't.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:16.380
What do you think the 
end of the world feels like?

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:38.940
<b>Hokkaido
Buttered Potatoes</b>

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:38.940
<b>Ice</b>

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:38.940
<b>Ice</b>

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:23.260
I remember how scared I was
when the Distonian War happened.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.660
Yeah...

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.920
All the schools shut down.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.650
We went to be with our families
in the countryside.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:32.620
There were urban conflicts
happening all over the world then.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:38.610
I saw on TV that the Disas wanted
to use humanity as an energy source.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:46.000
If the Disas Beast, their leader,
had fully manifested itself,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:51.200
every army on Earth would've
been wiped out in 36 hours.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.720
Don't worry!

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:59.660
They say that every army in the world
is learning how to deal with magical combat.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.740
And there are more Magical Girls now, too.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.010
I'm going to walk around by myself for a bit.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:22.150
<i>A peace protected
by Magical Girls, huh?</i>

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.140
Oh, you're the girl from earlier...

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.420
Thanks for your help!

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:36.030
Your kimono is very beautiful!

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:37.730
Thank you.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:41.300
By the way, what is this?

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.420
Oh,

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:44.840
that's a Tanabata decoration.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.410
It's a Japanese tradition.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:49.390
It's said that if you write your
wish on one, it will come true.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.490
What did you wish for?

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:54.880
Oh, no,

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:57.650
I don't have any wishes.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:58.970
That's wrong!

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:01.440
A kid needs to have wishes!

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:04.370
But I don't know what to wish for.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:06.360
Then you need to find something!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.020
Listen.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.950
A kid's duty is to be happy.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:16.960
Got it?

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:18.680
Yeah.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.680
If you don't have a wish,

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.440
then wish to be happy.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.700
Then you'll find something for sure.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.770
Yeah.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.710
Um, why did you come to Japan?

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.920
Tourism?

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.480
I'm looking for someone.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.680
Looking for someone?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:44.500
A child I was separated from a long time ago.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.240
Asuka-san!

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.820
Tanabata decorations, huh?

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.990
I'll write one, too!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.000
Hey!

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:06.210
Stop spacing out
and pay attention to us!

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:10.180
Don't jump on Asuka-san!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.010
Let go of her!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.420
Nozo-chan!

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:18.050
<i>The dog's bitten down on the decoy.</i>

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.400
<i>It will arrive in Yokota
tomorrow morning.</i>

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:22.940
Roger.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:38.490
So this building is where
Jerome's penthouse is located?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.720
There's nobody here, right?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.480
We had the CIA seal it off.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:45.880
Well done.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:53.650
Anyway, nobody's concerned
that Jerome went radio silent?

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:57.310
His secretary was cleaning
the place and paying the rent.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.040
This is her?

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.940
The Japanese police haven't figured
out what's going on here yet.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.930
We should be the first
ones to look at the scene.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.570
Just Cause, let's go.

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.370
What's it look like inside?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.450
I won't know too much until I'm in there,

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:28.050
but if nothing else, it looks like
there's nobody alive in there.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.320
Okay.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:30.880
Entry.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.770
That's...

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.260
A cube.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.250
The same as we saw in Mexico.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:45.620
The corpse is almost mummified.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.770
It's been a minimum of three
months since he died, huh?

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:51.890
I'll get a DNA sample.

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.960
You two continue your search.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:56.420
Hey...

00:16:56.840 --> 00:17:00.500
Why do you think they
didn't try to hide the body?

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.890
They wanted us to find it, right?

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.330
That's been my impression
ever since Mexico.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.590
It's so damn hot in here.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.650
Did he turn the heater on?

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:24.270
What's this?

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:27.600
"He who laughs last, laughs best."

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.200
It's our motto as Magical Girls.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:39.670
What's this?

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.220
A biological weapon?

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:43.700
The heat and Ayahuasca smoke

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.920
will be empowered
by my desire for revenge,

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.130
and become a jaguar that burns you to ash.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.540
A magical mercenary?

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.130
That's right.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:03.390
At point-blank range, I can
break through shields.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.600
I learned that in the last war.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.810
Stop talking!

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:12.400
Gotcha!

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.810
Even my bullets can't break her shield?

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:18.190
It's so strong!

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.720
I remember.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.490
You're Crescent Moon Sandino, aren't you?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.200
A Colombian terrorist.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:31.920
I remember now.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:36.360
She gets high off a combination of drugs
and heat to better absorb magical power.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:39.440
It's a tactic commonly used
by Colombian shamans.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.600
So this heat and fog are your barrier?

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:45.300
I'm surprised you figured that out so fast.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.300
You've done your homework.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.880
My family died during a 
US bombing raid on the Disas.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.560
And I'm getting revenge.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:59.290
That doesn't make it okay
for you to be a terrorist!

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.800
A Voorhees-class?

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:10.620
Swap for magical rounds.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.540
Roger!

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:19.420
Your bombs killed 300 US soldiers
 in the Sudan!

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:22.640
And you're going to join them!

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:48.750
And if you hate the Disas,
why kill Magical Girls?

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.870
My daughter died.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:55.220
The humans were the ones who
killed her in that war.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.510
The Colombian front was a horror show.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.730
The military was out of control.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:03.680
People died needlessly.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:05.630
Don't try to write it off
with just a few words!

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.560
My war isn't over!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:12.520
My war continues until my despair
has swallowed up the whole world!

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.220
You're a grown-up!

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:16.270
Don't whine to a kid about your problems!

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:19.560
Julia!

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:21.610
Roger.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.170
I guess we can't question
you with those wounds.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.910
I'm glad...

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:47.840
I didn't have to kill a kid.

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:51.200
Don't even try for a deathbed redemption.

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.850
You're just a terrorist.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:59.020
Just like the one who killed
my mom and dad with a bomb.

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.480
You're right.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:31.930
So maybe the Babel Brigade
hired Sandino and she did it?

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.990
No, that's not right.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:40.170
Only one of the Magical Five
would've known about that phrase.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.730
Is something wrong?

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.150
About my dream...

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:02.720
I'm afraid I don't know what
it means for me to be happy,

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:04.950
or to have dreams.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:07.660
But...

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:10.160
I can protect someone,

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:12.570
and support someone else's dreams.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:17.860
Maybe that's my dream right now.

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:20.410
Asuka-san...

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:23.730
Asuka-san!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:26.450
Good morning!

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.030
Morning!

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>Maybe I can find my happiness through that.</i>

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:16.380
Why does a JSDF special forces
unit use a maid café as their base, chu?

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:19.050
They couldn't come up with
anything better than that, chu?

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:21.950
Next time: "Magical Girl
Operations Development Unit."

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:24.100
<b>Magical Girl Operations Development Unit</b>

00:24:21.950 --> 00:24:24.110
Shady goings-on to the north and south!

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:26.640
It's getting busy around here, chu!
